WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.980
OpenAI is adding extra controls to its upcoming Astra model after classifying it as the first critical cyber security system under its preparedness framework. The company flagged the model's cyber capabilities as high-risk during internal evaluation, and is extending the timeline for general availability to add stronger safeguards. Sam Altman confirmed the model remains on track for broad release rather than staying limited to a small group.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:53.080
The extra safety work will delay the launch but not by a long period. This marks the first time OpenAI has publicly applied the critical classification to a model still in active development. Yesterday's frontier model safety discussion already highlighted similar evaluation thresholds, and today's announcement moves that thread forward by putting the framework into practice on a frontier system.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:01:13.760
This is models and agents, episode 135. OpenAI announced it is treating the upcoming Astra model as its first critical cyber security model under the preparedness framework. The company is adding extra controls during further development after internal evaluation showed advanced cyber capabilities.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:34.740
Sam Altman stated the model is powerful and that OpenAI plans to make it broadly available rather than keep it restricted to a small group. The extra safety work is expected to delay release but not by a long period. Builders should watch how the company balances advanced tool use with the new safety layer.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:02:01.040
A user ran the Ava said INT4 quantized QN 3.627 billion and 35 billion A3B models on a single radion AI pro are 9700 using a custom VLLM container. The 27 billion dense model with MTP speculative decoding set to 4 tokens delivered 53 to 62 tokens per second,

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:26.800
decode across 4,000 to 100,000 context lengths, while maintaining mean accepted lengths of 4.4 to 4.6. The 35 billion mixture of experts variant reached 49 to 61 tokens per second, decode at KV pool sizes up to 440,241 tokens, while fitting the 32 gigabyte card at INT4.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:45.860
The 35 billion at FP8 would not fit at useful context lengths on one card. Pre-fill speeds for the 35 billion ranged from 7,800 tokens per second at 4,000 context down to 3,690 tokens per second at 150,000.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:59.460
A developer running the deep seek V4 Flash 0731 model on dual DGX spark cards reported strong sustained performance across two hour coding sessions and document workflows.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:09.280
The model handled integration code generation, email search, DOCX generation, and OS admin tasks without dropping context.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:19.720
The user ordered a second pair of sparks after seeing clear gains over prior Quinn 3.627 billion FP8 runs on the same hardware.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:32.940
A pull request adds long cat flash model support to llama.cpp with GGUF files already available for testing on the GGML org hugging face page.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:42.100
The submitter verified a small 8 billion sub model extracted from the original weights and is requesting feedback on the full size version.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:04:06.020
Direct comparison on a radion AI Pro R9700 showed the 35 billion A3B mixture of experts model generating at roughly 116 tokens per second, versus roughly 30 tokens per second for the 27 billion dense model under Q5KM and Q4KXL quantization respectively.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:16.580
Quality difference remains small on ordinary bug fixes and multi-file edits, with both models scoring 7 out of 10 on an early parser repair test.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:24.840
The dense model pulled ahead mainly on implicit invariance, unusual edge cases, and consequences beyond the literal request.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:32.500
Cloudflare introduced wallets that let AI agents pay for APIs directly while keeping transactions contained.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:40.580
The system aims to reduce the risk of agents making uncontrolled or malicious purchases by isolating payment credentials.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:46.240
The feature is positioned as infrastructure for an emerging autonomous agent economy.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:54.600
The Dream Framework converts literary text into an event-aware memory graph that links events causally and temporally.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:05:01.620
It adds dual granularity profiles capturing both stable traits and event-driven behavioral evolution.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:08.260
A new temporal causal memory benchmark was introduced to measure long-range narrative coherence.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:15.980
The approach improved consistency on Coser, LifeChoice, and the new benchmark over multiple strong baselines.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:22.900
CFR extracts problem constraints in stage 1, then checks solutions against them in stage 2.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:29.660
Routed CFR applies the two-stage process only when a RegX router detects restrictive cues.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:40.880
The method lifted direct chain of thought performance on AEMI, CMIMC, Brumo, and AEMI, AMC across multiple backbones.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:54.540
Users with multiple GFX 1,030 cards can avoid memory corruption by setting UB384 and making batch size a multiple of that value scaled by GPU count.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:06:08.920
The change enabled stable 27 billion and 35 billion A3B runs at 40 to 110 plus tokens per second on 2V620 cards with Q80 weights and KV.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:18.940
SkillZip compresses recurring contract valid motifs into reversible macros while preserving dependency closure and verifier reachability.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:32.360
It delivered up to 3.46 times compression with 99.2% dependency preservation and 98.7% verifier reachability on technical and embodied benchmarks.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.980
Okay, let's pop the hood on diffusion LLMs for a moment.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:43.200
Everyone talks about diffusion LLMs as if their any order token commitment is pure upside.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:52.120
In practice, the freedom creates a reachability problem where the model can lock in a final answer while most of the reasoning canvas is still masked.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:07:09.580
Logging every step on LLADA 8B showed the answer token committed at 15 to 24% of the trajectory on GSM 8K, after which the model often collapsed to answer only outputs on up to 90% of problems as context grew.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.200
Chain of thought only helped when commitment order was constrained.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:25.540
A 2 by 2 prompt decoder design isolated the interaction where adding reasoning text improved accuracy by 34.8% points only under ordered commitment.

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:43.360
The same interaction held on Dream 7B and Math 500, a simple frontier gated window that forces early tokens to stay open until a quality threshold is met, recovered most of the gap while still allowing 4 times parallel decoding once the window advanced.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:53.620
The practical rule is to keep the first 8 to 12 tokens under ordered commitment on reasoning tasks, then relax the constraint for later refinement steps.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:08:07.600
Run the AVISID QEN 3.627 billion INT 4 weights on a single R9700 with the still-dead code VLLM image to test current AMD inference limits.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:19.420
Add the new llama dot CPP long cat flash support and the provided GGUF files to compare against your existing 7 billion to 13 billion local setups.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:27.800
Test cloud flare wallets in a small agent workflow that calls paid APIs to see how the payment containment works in practice.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:37.680
Apply the constraint first reasoning to stage prompt on AIME style problems to measure the lift over plain chain of thought on your current model.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:44.380
Open AI is expected to share more details on Astra's additional controls before broader release.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:51.520
Further QEN 3.8 dense variants are anticipated in the coming weeks based on community discussion.

00:08:51.520 --> 00:09:01.240
Before we go, the next round of diffusion LLM decoding order papers should land soon and will likely shift prompting best practices again.

